{% extends 'site/guideBase.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Fleets</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                Fleets allow you to move units between your own regions. This is separate from
                <a href="{{ url('Guide/Attack') }}">attacking</a>, which sends units to enemy regions.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Sending Units</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>To move units between your regions:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Click on one of your regions on the <a href="{{ url('Guide/World') }}">world map</a>.</li>
                <li>Select the units you want to send.</li>
                <li>Choose a target region (must be another region you own).</li>
                <li>The units will form a fleet and travel to the target.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>
                Travel time is based on the distance between the source and target regions.
                You can send Troops, Air Units, Naval Units, and Missiles.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Fleet Actions</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>Active fleets are shown on the world map and in the fleet panel:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>Recall:</b> Cancel a fleet that is still traveling. The units return to the source region immediately.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Reinforce:</b> When a fleet arrives at your region, you can reinforce to add the units to the region's garrison.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                The fleet panel shows each fleet's source and target coordinates, the units being transported, and the estimated time of arrival.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
